      },
      "oauth2": {
        "description": "OAuth2 authorization code flow (RFC 6749) with PKCE (RFC 7636) and rotating refresh tokens, for third-party applications (including MCP integrations) acting on behalf of a consenting user. It uses an Org API token with `oauth_enabled` set as the OAuth2 client, the `client_id` is its composite `oauth_client_id` (`<org_id>.<token_id>`). See the [Orgs OAuth2](/#operations/getOauthAuthorization) endpoints.\n\n**Format**:\n  `Authorization: Bearer {access_token}`\n\n**Notes**:\n* The access token carries the privileges configured on the API token, constrained to what the consenting user has\n* The access token expires after `oauth_ttl` (default 1 hour), use the refresh token to get a new one\n* No fixed scopes are defined, the scope is derived from the API token name (e.g. `custom-ServiceNow Integration`)",
        "flows": {
